{
  // Cloudflare Workers static-assets deploy for reynaldiwong.com.
  //
  // Assets-only: there is no Worker script, and `main` is optional for assets-only Workers.
  // `directory: "./"` because the site is build-free - it ships from the repo root, and
  // there is no ./dist to point at.
  //
  // not_found_handling "404-page" makes Workers answer an unmatched path with the nearest
  // 404.html and a real 404 status, so tools/serve.py is only needed for local work.
  //
  // _headers IS honoured here. It is documented under Pages, but the Workers static-assets
  // headers docs (updated 2026-08-25) say the same thing verbatim: the file "will instead
  // be parsed by Workers and its rules will be applied to static asset responses". The one
  // limit is that _headers rules do not apply to responses generated by Worker code - and
  // there is no Worker code here, so the CSP/HSTS/nosniff block does apply.
  //
  // No "$schema" key on purpose: it would point at ./node_modules/wrangler/..., and this
  // repo has no node_modules (wrangler runs via npx).
  //
  // LOCAL DEV FOOTGUN: because directory is "./", the assets directory CONTAINS .wrangler/,
  // where wrangler dev keeps its state. It watches that directory, so its own state writes
  // retrigger it - `wrangler dev` sits in an endless "Reloading local server..." loop and
  // never answers a request. Point the state elsewhere for local work:
  //
  //   npx wrangler dev --persist-to /tmp/wrangler-state
  //
  // Verified both ways: state inside the tree never served a request; with --persist-to
  // outside it, requests were served immediately and _headers was applied.
  "name": "reynaldi-website",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-12",
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./",
    "not_found_handling": "404-page"
  }
}
